  "title": "Counting is polynomial on every three-fold space",
  "subject": "The number of 2-colourings of a three-fold space with one line removed",
  "conclusion": "For every three-fold space the colourings with one line removed are counted in polynomial time without any signing: a product over braces, a planar brace one Berman determinant, any other brace a Robertson-Seymour-Thomas trisum tree evaluated with two weighted determinants per planar leaf. Exact counts reach 1720-vertex instances where variable elimination would need factors on 30 variables.",
